# `tsc` output. The gate RUNS `dist/`, but it is rebuilt by `npm run build` on
# every invocation — a committed copy would be a second source of truth for the
# same code, and the stale one always wins an argument.
dist/
dist*/

# The emitted per-atom row list (`npm run emitted-atoms`) — a MEASUREMENT, not a
# source. Regenerated by re-running the leg; a committed copy would be a second
# source of truth for a number the leg exists to take.
.atoms/

# The TERMINAL SEAL PREIMAGE (`npm run head-anchor-pins -- --emit`) — the
# `friCommit`/`accOutDigest` a `DreggHeadGate` caller exhibits. A MEASUREMENT of
# whichever chain `.fullchain/` currently holds, and it rotates with every
# re-emit of the descriptors. A committed copy would be a second source of truth
# for two fields that look authoritative and go stale silently, which is the one
# way this artifact can hurt: the run that regenerates it is a single command and
# it records that command in itself.
dregg-chain-seal.json

# The process-per-slice chain's boundary artifacts (`npm run root-air-fullchain`)
# — proofs, verification keys and feature flags handed between processes. They
# are the RUN, not a source; the leg clears and re-mints them unless
# `FULLCHAIN_REUSE=1`, which no gate run sets.
.fullchain/
